{"id":"e136714944ab7f793307d7685e306b2383f2f310","axis":"silent","repo":"PrefectHQ/prefect","sha":"e136714944ab7f793307d7685e306b2383f2f310","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"src/prefect/cli/AGENTS.md","lines":["@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ Prefect command-line interface, powered by **cyclopts**."," "," - **Use `rich` for all output.** Console output via `rich.console`, tables via `rich.table`, progress bars via `rich.progress`. Always use `exit_with_error` for error exits."," - **Support JSON output whenever possible.** Commands should have a `--json` flag or equivalent for machine-readable output. Any diagnostic or informational `print()` calls must be suppressed when JSON output is active — mixing human-readable text with the JSON payload breaks machine consumers.","-- **Print JSON and other verbatim user data with `markup=False, emoji=False`.** `console.print` otherwise parses `[...]` as Rich markup and `:name:` as emoji aliases, silently rewriting payloads (or raising `MarkupError` on stray closing tags). `print_json` and `Pretty` are not affected.","+- **Print JSON, YAML, and other verbatim user data with `print_verbatim` from `_utilities.py`.** `console.print` otherwise parses `[...]` as Rich markup and `:name:` as emoji aliases, silently rewriting payloads (or raising `MarkupError` on stray closing tags). `print_verbatim` disables both and soft-wraps; `tests/cli/test_utilities.py` fails if serialized output goes through `console.print` directly. `print_json` and `Pretty` are not affected."," - **Page through \"all records\" reads.** Client `read_*` list calls without `limit` return at most `PREFECT_SERVER_API_DEFAULT_LIMIT` (200) rows (server `LimitBody`) — or fewer when the client method has its own default `limit` (e.g. `read_global_concurrency_limits` defaults to 10) — so `--all`/bulk commands must loop on `offset`. When deleting while paging, re-read from offset 0 each pass — advancing `offset` skips rows that shifted into earlier pages."," - **Excluded from `prefect-client`** — the entire `cli/` directory is stripped during the client package build."," "],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/prefect/cli/_utilities.py","lines":["@@ -28,6 +28,17 @@ def exit_with_success(message: str, **kwargs: Any) -> NoReturn:","     raise SystemExit(0)"," "," ","+def print_verbatim(output: str) -> None:","+    \"\"\"","+    Print machine-readable output (e.g. JSON or YAML) exactly as given.","+","+    Rich markup and emoji alias parsing are disabled so user data like","+    `[red]text[/red]` or `:smile:` is not rewritten, and soft wrapping keeps","+    long lines intact.","+    \"\"\"","+    _cli.console.print(output, soft_wrap=True, markup=False, emoji=False)","+","+"," def with_cli_exception_handling(fn: Callable[..., Any]) -> Callable[..., Any]:","     if inspect.iscoroutinefunction(fn):"," "],"additions":11,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"src/prefect/cli/artifact.py","lines":["@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@"," from prefect.cli._utilities import (","     exit_with_error,","     exit_with_success,","+    print_verbatim,","     with_cli_exception_handling,"," )"," ","@@ -77,7 +78,7 @@ async def list_artifacts(","     if output and output.lower() == \"json\":","         artifacts_json = [artifact.model_dump(mode=\"json\") for artifact in artifacts]","         json_output = orjson.dumps(artifacts_json, option=orjson.OPT_INDENT_2).decode()","-        _cli.console.print(json_output, soft_wrap=True, markup=False, emoji=False)","+        print_verbatim(json_output)","     else:","         table = Table(","             title=\"Artifacts\",","@@ -181,7 +182,7 @@ async def inspect(","             json_output = orjson.dumps(","                 artifacts_json, option=orjson.OPT_INDENT_2","             ).decode()","-            _cli.console.print(json_output, soft_wrap=True, markup=False, emoji=False)","+            print_verbatim(json_output)","         else:","             _cli.console.print(Pretty(artifacts_json))"," "],"additions":3,"de